    "title": "What’s open and closed on Patriots’ Day in Massachusetts?",
    "text": "Patriots’ Day is not a Federal holiday. by: Emma McCorkindale Posted: Apr 20, 2026 / 09:17 AM EDT Updated: Apr 20, 2026 / 09:17 AM EDT CHICOPEE, Mass. (WWLP) – Monday is Patriots’ Day, which means some Americans will mark the beginning of the nation’s war for independence. Patriots’ Day was first celebrated in Massachusetts back in 1894. It was proclaimed by then-governor Frederic Greenhalge to diffuse a rivalry between Lexington and Concord who had dueling celebrations to mark the start of the American Revolution. This state holiday can affect the availability of services in the states that celebrate it. Patriots’ Day is not a Federal holiday, so Federal offices, including the Post Office, will be open. Banks may be open as well as retail stores. Target and Walmart will be open. The MBTA will run on its standard weekday schedule. State, county, municipal offices, and RMVs in the states that celebrate will be closed on Patriots’ Day, as well as schools and libraries. Local News Headlines WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Download the 22News Plus app on your TV to watch live-streaming newscasts and video on demand.",
